# patches.md — start.bat Error Report & Fixes

## Run date: 2026-05-21

---

## Bug 1 — Gateway never binds port 8642 (readiness loop always times out)

**Symptom**  
`start.bat` launches `hermes gateway run` then polls `netstat` for `:8642` for up to 30 seconds. The gateway process starts successfully but port 8642 never opens, so the loop always exhausts and prints:

```
Warning: Gateway may still be starting -- check logs in %USERPROFILE%\.hermes\logs\
```

**Root cause**  
Port 8642 is the Hermes API server, which is an **opt-in** platform. It only binds when `API_SERVER_ENABLED=true` is set in the environment or `.env`. The original `start.bat` launched the gateway without this variable, so the gateway ran in cron+messaging-only mode and never opened port 8642.

The Desktop app's own `startGateway()` (Desktop/src/main/hermes.ts:1087) correctly sets `API_SERVER_ENABLED: "true"` — the bat script was missing this.

**Fix applied** (`start.bat`)  
Added `set API_SERVER_ENABLED=true` before the gateway launch line so port 8642 binds and the readiness check succeeds.

